    "reviews": "\u201c&quot;Ayasa: Shadows of Silence\u2018s world feels somewhat similar, blending a mix of traditional fantasy vistas with eerie, Little Nightmares-style themes. For me, it was an immediate wishlist based purely on its aesthetic alone.&quot;\u201d<br>Lauren Bergin from PCGAMESN<br><br>\u201c''If you\u2019re hankering for an indie horror experience akin to Little Nightmares, I think I\u2019ve found it. A first look at Ayasa: Shadow of Silence dropped today, an upcoming platformer blending exploration, puzzles, and horror to deliver a spooky narrative-driven experience.''\u201d<br>Alex Gibson from Nerd Stash<br><br>\u201c''Ayasa, Shadows of Silence has a creepiness of its own, combined with its own brand of gameplay.''\u201d<br>Mike Wilson from Bloody Disgusting<br>",
